1
00:00:09,277 --> 00:00:11,927
=The Glory Fades 2=

2
00:00:11,927 --> 00:00:13,798
=Episode 17=

3
00:00:14,770 --> 00:00:15,770
Mr. Envoy,

4
00:00:16,427 --> 00:00:17,547
the border bandit problem

5
00:00:17,547 --> 00:00:19,227
didn't happen overnight,

6
00:00:19,586 --> 00:00:21,066
but it's not unsolvable.

7
00:00:21,346 --> 00:00:22,826
My stance is clear:

8
00:00:23,266 --> 00:00:24,266
strike hard

9
00:00:24,426 --> 00:00:25,427
and show no leniency.

10
00:00:25,986 --> 00:00:26,986
Whoever makes trouble

11
00:00:27,186 --> 00:00:28,267
will be taken down.

12
00:00:29,427 --> 00:00:32,307
Relying on force alone
will only alienate the border people.

13
00:00:32,587 --> 00:00:35,067
Security and livelihood
are two sides of the same coin.

14
00:00:35,467 --> 00:00:36,506
Guns alone

15
00:00:36,666 --> 00:00:37,866
won't solve the root problem.

16
00:00:38,826 --> 00:00:40,866
Mr. Tang, you just returned from ASEAN,

17
00:00:40,866 --> 00:00:43,467
so you may not grasp
our current reality.

18
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:45,707
For rebels in the north,

19
00:00:45,866 --> 00:00:48,067
unless we teach them a lesson,

20
00:00:48,427 --> 00:00:50,667
they'll only push for more.

21
00:00:50,667 --> 00:00:52,506
I agree we shouldn't be lenient.

22
00:00:52,747 --> 00:00:54,506
But our approach can be smarter.

23
00:00:54,626 --> 00:00:56,787
Let's reassure the public first,
then eliminate them.

24
00:00:56,787 --> 00:00:57,906
That'll work better.

25
00:01:04,027 --> 00:01:05,027
Mr. Envoy,

26
00:01:05,427 --> 00:01:07,467
oysters are our local specialty.

27
00:01:07,946 --> 00:01:10,826
Let's talk maritime over seafood.
Have a taste.

28
00:01:10,826 --> 00:01:11,826
Sure.

29
00:01:20,466 --> 00:01:22,506
Switch to this. Burgundy.

30
00:01:23,427 --> 00:01:25,267
Ms. Bai, according to the original plan,

31
00:01:25,267 --> 00:01:26,827
it's time for sake.

32
00:01:26,866 --> 00:01:28,427
I'm in charge of the drinks.

33
00:01:28,827 --> 00:01:30,787
I say we switch, so we switch.

34
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:42,226
Mr. Envoy,

35
00:01:42,466 --> 00:01:43,466
please.

36
00:01:49,627 --> 00:01:53,026
Regarding Mr. Nie's call
for hard suppression,

37
00:01:53,026 --> 00:01:56,226
personally, I admire
your country's determination.

38
00:01:56,627 --> 00:01:59,427
However, if your government forces

39
00:01:59,466 --> 00:02:02,226
can't eradicate the bandits
in the short term,

40
00:02:02,787 --> 00:02:06,666
our side can provide
technical military support,

41
00:02:06,666 --> 00:02:08,386
including naval drills

42
00:02:08,386 --> 00:02:10,827
and joint border operations.

43
00:02:17,746 --> 00:02:18,746
Mr. Envoy,

44
00:02:19,066 --> 00:02:20,346
allow me to emphasize:

45
00:02:21,026 --> 00:02:23,186
we can discuss port security cooperation

46
00:02:23,346 --> 00:02:24,667
and intelligence sharing,

47
00:02:25,026 --> 00:02:26,827
but allowing foreign military forces

48
00:02:26,827 --> 00:02:28,306
onto our soil

49
00:02:28,346 --> 00:02:30,987
is entirely non-negotiable.

50
00:02:31,227 --> 00:02:33,026
Our country doesn't need anyone

51
00:02:33,387 --> 00:02:35,827
telling us how to govern our own land.

52
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:38,667
Very well.

53
00:02:39,427 --> 00:02:41,707
Then please give us a timeline, Mr. Nie.

54
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:42,786
Three months?

55
00:02:42,866 --> 00:02:43,866
Six months?

56
00:02:43,987 --> 00:02:46,227
Or should we wait
until your election ends

57
00:02:46,227 --> 00:02:47,827
for the new speaker to handle it?

58
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:53,427
Sure, we can set a timeline,

59
00:02:53,547 --> 00:02:56,626
but not as a casual
dinner promise, right?

60
00:02:56,626 --> 00:02:59,427
I propose forming a trilateral
economic security group

61
00:02:59,466 --> 00:03:00,866
of the Royal Family, the Cabinet,

62
00:03:00,866 --> 00:03:02,947
and Dongdao corporate delegates.

63
00:03:02,947 --> 00:03:04,066
We handle security,

64
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:05,427
and you provide investment.

65
00:03:05,586 --> 00:03:07,186
We solve border issues through projects,

66
00:03:07,186 --> 00:03:08,186
not through

67
00:03:08,227 --> 00:03:09,267
military force.

68
00:03:11,987 --> 00:03:12,987
Tang,

69
00:03:13,667 --> 00:03:14,746
you're quite pragmatic.

70
00:03:14,746 --> 00:03:15,746
Cheers.

71
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:26,186
- Are you alright?
- I'm fine.

72
00:03:26,186 --> 00:03:27,866
I just can't handle my liquor.

73
00:03:31,026 --> 00:03:32,827
Mr. Envoy, what's wrong?

74
00:03:33,026 --> 00:03:35,306
It's fine.
My stomach just hurts suddenly.

75
00:03:35,466 --> 00:03:36,466
Nothing serious.

76
00:03:37,466 --> 00:03:39,306
We just finished
discussing border issues,

77
00:03:39,786 --> 00:03:41,387
and now this happens to him.

78
00:03:41,387 --> 00:03:42,507
Is this a coincidence

79
00:03:42,626 --> 00:03:43,667
or a warning?

80
00:03:44,066 --> 00:03:46,427
If this was your intentional move,

81
00:03:46,466 --> 00:03:48,827
it's an open provocation
against our envoy.

82
00:03:49,026 --> 00:03:51,667
If you can't even guarantee the safety

83
00:03:51,667 --> 00:03:53,586
of an envoy,

84
00:03:53,586 --> 00:03:55,786
we will have to reassess

85
00:03:55,786 --> 00:03:58,066
our investments in your land

86
00:03:58,387 --> 00:03:59,466
and border cooperation

87
00:03:59,987 --> 00:04:02,466
and escalate our security measures.

88
00:04:05,387 --> 00:04:06,387
Come here.

89
00:04:09,066 --> 00:04:11,066
You were in charge of tonight's dinner.

90
00:04:11,267 --> 00:04:12,427
What on earth happened?

91
00:04:13,267 --> 00:04:14,267
Your Highness,

92
00:04:14,427 --> 00:04:16,466
the problem must be
with Su Yunian's dishes.

93
00:04:17,227 --> 00:04:18,586
She set the menu

94
00:04:18,586 --> 00:04:20,227
and checked the ingredients.

95
00:04:20,947 --> 00:04:22,427
Now that the envoy is unwell,

96
00:04:23,387 --> 00:04:24,466
she's definitely to blame.

97
00:04:24,466 --> 00:04:26,867
I checked all the ingredients
at least three times.

98
00:04:26,867 --> 00:04:28,947
I even avoided any potential allergens.

99
00:04:28,947 --> 00:04:30,026
I kept samples.

100
00:04:30,026 --> 00:04:31,026
You can check them.

101
00:04:31,147 --> 00:04:32,507
Saying so proves nothing.

102
00:04:32,546 --> 00:04:34,307
Who knows if you tampered

103
00:04:34,307 --> 00:04:35,627
with the retained samples?

104
00:04:35,827 --> 00:04:36,827
Su Yunian,

105
00:04:36,867 --> 00:04:38,986
the Grand Princess and I
trusted you so much.

106
00:04:39,627 --> 00:04:41,226
Is this how you do your job?

107
00:04:41,666 --> 00:04:42,867
Feng, I...

108
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:43,867
Feng,

109
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:45,507
don't jump to conclusions.

110
00:04:48,346 --> 00:04:49,346
What are you doing here?

111
00:04:49,747 --> 00:04:51,906
I'm the former
assistant manager of Prosperity.

112
00:04:52,426 --> 00:04:54,786
Prosperity handled tonight's dinner,

113
00:04:54,786 --> 00:04:56,187
so why can't I be here?

114
00:04:58,947 --> 00:04:59,947
Jiasheng,

115
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:01,627
what do you want?

116
00:05:07,867 --> 00:05:08,867
Envoy.

117
00:05:10,627 --> 00:05:12,026
This isn't food poisoning.

118
00:05:12,426 --> 00:05:13,827
It's an allergic reaction.

119
00:05:13,867 --> 00:05:15,986
The envoy's allergy list
was sent to you long ago.

120
00:05:15,986 --> 00:05:17,747
Don't worry. I thoroughly checked

121
00:05:17,747 --> 00:05:20,187
every item on that list.
Everything was fine.

122
00:05:20,187 --> 00:05:21,307
It's not the ingredients.

123
00:05:31,226 --> 00:05:32,986
The problem lies with this wine.

124
00:05:32,986 --> 00:05:34,426
Burgundy Grand Cru

125
00:05:34,627 --> 00:05:35,666
is aged in barrels

126
00:05:35,666 --> 00:05:36,947
made of ironwood berry trees.

127
00:05:36,947 --> 00:05:37,947
The wine itself contains

128
00:05:38,026 --> 00:05:39,546
trace amounts of berry phenols.

129
00:05:39,546 --> 00:05:41,867
But I'm not allergic
to ironwood berries.

130
00:05:41,867 --> 00:05:43,067
You're indeed not.

131
00:05:43,187 --> 00:05:44,986
Drinking this wine alone is harmless,

132
00:05:45,147 --> 00:05:46,786
and eating oysters alone is fine.

133
00:05:46,827 --> 00:05:48,067
But combined,

134
00:05:48,346 --> 00:05:50,387
they form a new complex protein.

135
00:05:50,387 --> 00:05:53,226
You're likely allergic
to that complex protein.

136
00:05:53,267 --> 00:05:56,546
Don't worry. The reaction
should pass in ten minutes.

137
00:05:56,747 --> 00:05:59,466
Ms. Bai, sake was supposed
to follow the oysters.

138
00:05:59,466 --> 00:06:01,827
Why did you switch
to this red wine on your own?

139
00:06:01,827 --> 00:06:02,827
I...

140
00:06:04,867 --> 00:06:05,986
I just felt sake

141
00:06:05,986 --> 00:06:07,267
was plain for a state dinner.

142
00:06:07,267 --> 00:06:09,026
That's why I switched to this wine.

143
00:06:09,747 --> 00:06:11,627
How could I have known any of this?

144
00:06:11,986 --> 00:06:13,867
Who gave you the nerve
to act on your own?

145
00:06:13,986 --> 00:06:14,986
Ms. Bai

146
00:06:15,187 --> 00:06:17,067
had no reason to target the envoy.

147
00:06:17,267 --> 00:06:18,267
I'm sure

148
00:06:18,267 --> 00:06:19,627
it was just an oversight.

149
00:06:19,627 --> 00:06:20,627
An oversight?

150
00:06:20,867 --> 00:06:22,586
An oversight is still on you.

151
00:06:22,586 --> 00:06:24,466
Given the envoy's current condition,

152
00:06:24,466 --> 00:06:26,947
I suggest canceling all remaining talks

153
00:06:26,947 --> 00:06:28,067
and returning home now.

154
00:06:28,466 --> 00:06:31,986
Envoy, Prosperity bears
all the blame today,

155
00:06:31,986 --> 00:06:34,666
so Prosperity will give you
an explanation.

156
00:06:35,026 --> 00:06:36,026
Rather than blame,

157
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:37,666
I'd like to bring up another matter,

158
00:06:37,666 --> 00:06:38,666
one that

159
00:06:38,947 --> 00:06:40,867
can make up for all this unpleasantness.

160
00:06:41,466 --> 00:06:42,466
What matter?

161
00:06:42,546 --> 00:06:43,546
Your country

162
00:06:43,627 --> 00:06:45,586
has always imported crude oil from Yapu,

163
00:06:46,026 --> 00:06:47,026
passing through

164
00:06:47,426 --> 00:06:48,426
two checkpoints

165
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:49,867
and three ports.

166
00:06:49,947 --> 00:06:52,026
All tariffs, insurance,
and freight costs

167
00:06:52,267 --> 00:06:54,026
add up to a considerable expense.

168
00:06:54,026 --> 00:06:55,906
Instead of talking
border security, why not

169
00:06:56,387 --> 00:06:57,507
sign a trilateral deal?

170
00:07:02,466 --> 00:07:04,426
We provide cold chains, ports,

171
00:07:04,426 --> 00:07:05,627
and road transit.

172
00:07:05,747 --> 00:07:07,067
Yapu supplies the crude oil,

173
00:07:07,067 --> 00:07:09,226
and your country provides
technology and funds.

174
00:07:09,226 --> 00:07:10,507
A trilateral cooperation

175
00:07:10,666 --> 00:07:12,867
is far more worthwhile
and far more enduring

176
00:07:13,187 --> 00:07:14,187
than just border security.

177
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,627
If this trilateral cooperation

178
00:07:15,627 --> 00:07:18,226
can truly be realized as you said,

179
00:07:18,346 --> 00:07:21,187
I can treat today's incident
as a misunderstanding

180
00:07:21,546 --> 00:07:22,546
that never happened.

181
00:07:22,666 --> 00:07:25,627
However, why would Yapu agree?

182
00:07:25,786 --> 00:07:26,786
For that,

183
00:07:27,267 --> 00:07:28,267
we'll have to rely on

184
00:07:28,346 --> 00:07:29,346
Secretary-General

185
00:07:29,426 --> 00:07:30,507
Tang Niansen.

186
00:07:32,267 --> 00:07:33,827
During your time at ASEAN,

187
00:07:33,986 --> 00:07:35,867
you were close
with Yapu's foreign envoy.

188
00:07:36,147 --> 00:07:38,067
Coincidentally, that former envoy

189
00:07:38,067 --> 00:07:40,387
is now Yapu's
director of the Energy Bureau.

190
00:07:40,387 --> 00:07:41,466
I can make the call,

191
00:07:41,466 --> 00:07:43,426
but I can't guarantee

192
00:07:43,867 --> 00:07:45,026
they'll agree.

193
00:07:45,026 --> 00:07:48,067
No problem. Just make the call,
and I'll handle the rest.

194
00:07:48,067 --> 00:07:49,067
Alright.

195
00:07:53,466 --> 00:07:54,707
What's your name?

196
00:07:55,586 --> 00:07:56,586
Tu Jiasheng.

197
00:07:57,627 --> 00:07:58,707
I'll remember you.

198
00:07:58,707 --> 00:07:59,707
Good.

199
00:08:04,226 --> 00:08:06,267
Yapu has tentatively agreed

200
00:08:06,267 --> 00:08:07,827
to direct crude oil supply,

201
00:08:07,827 --> 00:08:09,707
port cold chains, and overland transit

202
00:08:09,707 --> 00:08:11,067
as the cooperation framework.

203
00:08:11,426 --> 00:08:12,906
Specific terms can be negotiated,

204
00:08:13,026 --> 00:08:14,026
and they are willing

205
00:08:14,187 --> 00:08:15,187
to come to the table.

206
00:08:15,867 --> 00:08:16,867
Wonderful.

207
00:08:19,147 --> 00:08:20,786
Since there's mutual interest,

208
00:08:21,187 --> 00:08:22,187
envoy,

209
00:08:22,187 --> 00:08:24,267
let's move to the side hall
to talk details.

210
00:08:24,346 --> 00:08:25,346
Very well.

211
00:08:28,187 --> 00:08:29,466
You don't need to follow.

212
00:08:30,147 --> 00:08:31,786
Investigate today's incident thoroughly.

213
00:08:31,947 --> 00:08:33,147
See if it was an oversight

214
00:08:33,906 --> 00:08:34,906
or intentional.

215
00:08:35,307 --> 00:08:36,307
Yes.

216
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:50,946
Feng,

217
00:08:51,107 --> 00:08:52,906
I... I really didn't. Believe me.

218
00:08:53,267 --> 00:08:54,987
I just wanted to serve better wine.

219
00:08:54,987 --> 00:08:56,066
I meant the envoy no harm.

220
00:08:56,066 --> 00:08:57,826
Harming him would do me no good.

221
00:08:57,826 --> 00:08:59,826
You indeed had no reason
to target the envoy

222
00:08:59,946 --> 00:09:01,306
nor the guts.

223
00:09:01,306 --> 00:09:02,306
Because

224
00:09:02,387 --> 00:09:03,946
your target was Secretary-General Tang.

225
00:09:03,946 --> 00:09:05,906
Ridiculous! Give me one reason.

226
00:09:05,987 --> 00:09:07,186
Because you knew

227
00:09:07,186 --> 00:09:08,786
he was allergic to ironwood berries,

228
00:09:08,786 --> 00:09:10,706
and you switched
to this wine on purpose.

229
00:09:10,747 --> 00:09:12,666
How would I know what he's allergic to?

230
00:09:13,186 --> 00:09:15,706
Prosperity's records contain

231
00:09:15,706 --> 00:09:17,826
every regular guest's allergies

232
00:09:18,026 --> 00:09:19,026
and dietary restrictions.

233
00:09:19,747 --> 00:09:20,747
You haven't seen them?

234
00:09:20,826 --> 00:09:21,826
I haven't.

235
00:09:22,267 --> 00:09:23,426
Feng, I swear I haven't.

236
00:09:24,267 --> 00:09:25,666
Then why is Tang Niansen fine?

237
00:09:25,666 --> 00:09:27,467
I watched him drink it with my own eyes.

238
00:09:27,627 --> 00:09:29,666
You think Bai Ruxue will act
at the state dinner?

239
00:09:29,826 --> 00:09:31,026
Does she have the nerve?

240
00:09:31,026 --> 00:09:32,786
She wouldn't dare touch the envoy,

241
00:09:33,347 --> 00:09:35,666
but she'll definitely
target Tang Niansen.

242
00:09:37,786 --> 00:09:38,786
If she does this,

243
00:09:38,946 --> 00:09:40,946
she'll humiliate Tang Niansen
at the dinner

244
00:09:40,946 --> 00:09:42,147
and force him to leave early,

245
00:09:42,147 --> 00:09:43,906
leaving Nie Feng to take all the credit

246
00:09:44,666 --> 00:09:46,066
while framing Su Yunian.

247
00:09:46,227 --> 00:09:47,227
Two birds with one stone.

248
00:09:47,826 --> 00:09:49,587
Should we take precautions beforehand?

249
00:09:51,467 --> 00:09:53,227
Well, I'll call him and tell him

250
00:09:53,227 --> 00:09:54,546
to have his allergy meds ready

251
00:09:54,546 --> 00:09:55,546
and nudge things our way.

252
00:09:58,946 --> 00:09:59,946
Useless!

253
00:10:08,227 --> 00:10:09,227
Don't try it.

254
00:10:21,867 --> 00:10:22,867
Nie Feng,

255
00:10:23,227 --> 00:10:24,786
if word of today gets out,

256
00:10:25,026 --> 00:10:26,467
it benefits no one.

257
00:10:26,587 --> 00:10:27,587
Discipline

258
00:10:27,786 --> 00:10:29,026
your own people.

259
00:10:29,946 --> 00:10:30,946
Tu Jiasheng,

260
00:10:31,786 --> 00:10:33,267
you did well today.

261
00:10:33,666 --> 00:10:34,786
It's more fitting

262
00:10:34,867 --> 00:10:37,107
for you to run Prosperity.

263
00:10:40,666 --> 00:10:41,666
Nie Feng,

264
00:10:41,987 --> 00:10:43,026
any objections?

265
00:10:45,107 --> 00:10:46,107
Jiasheng

266
00:10:46,426 --> 00:10:48,267
is indeed better at that.

267
00:11:03,546 --> 00:11:04,546
Jiasheng,

268
00:11:05,147 --> 00:11:07,026
not only did you undercut me today,

269
00:11:09,467 --> 00:11:10,826
you went after my people.

270
00:11:11,306 --> 00:11:12,306
Feng,

271
00:11:12,946 --> 00:11:14,387
I wasn't undercutting you.

272
00:11:15,227 --> 00:11:16,507
I was protecting Prosperity

273
00:11:17,227 --> 00:11:18,306
and protecting you.

274
00:11:18,627 --> 00:11:20,426
If the envoy had pursued what happened,

275
00:11:20,426 --> 00:11:22,426
who do you think
the Grand Princess would blame?

276
00:11:22,666 --> 00:11:23,666
Prosperity,

277
00:11:23,666 --> 00:11:24,666
and above all, you.

278
00:11:24,747 --> 00:11:26,786
You're at a critical moment
in your campaign.

279
00:11:26,786 --> 00:11:29,426
Any diplomatic scandal
would be fatal to you.

280
00:11:30,426 --> 00:11:31,826
I warded off a disaster for you

281
00:11:32,186 --> 00:11:33,267
and stabilized Prosperity.

282
00:11:33,587 --> 00:11:34,867
It will only benefit you.

283
00:11:43,747 --> 00:11:44,747
Jiasheng,

284
00:11:45,066 --> 00:11:46,066
thank you.

285
00:11:47,826 --> 00:11:49,306
You did nothing wrong.

286
00:11:51,906 --> 00:11:52,906
Let's go.

287
00:11:53,026 --> 00:11:54,026
Back to Prosperity.

288
00:12:15,232 --> 00:12:18,848
♪Streetlights stretch shadows long♪

289
00:12:19,218 --> 00:12:23,203
♪As crowds fade,
who lingers on the edge♪

290
00:12:27,959 --> 00:12:31,278
♪Guarding all those unfinished lies♪

291
00:12:31,278 --> 00:12:36,363
♪Wind sweeps through the empty harbor♪

292
00:12:39,952 --> 00:12:46,504
♪Time quietly strips away the madness♪

293
00:12:46,504 --> 00:12:54,925
♪Plunging all passion
into freezing cold♪

294
00:12:54,925 --> 00:12:58,154
♪The feast ends, leaving only emptiness♪

295
00:12:58,154 --> 00:13:01,349
♪The past drifts far away, unstoppable♪

296
00:13:01,349 --> 00:13:04,042
♪If regret is an inescapable wandering♪

297
00:13:04,042 --> 00:13:08,659
♪I swallow the silence, burning alone♪

298
00:13:12,570 --> 00:13:15,059
♪Burning alone♪

299
00:13:20,565 --> 00:13:26,934
♪The glory fades♪
